   "title": "Improving an Explanation",
   "mode": "listen",
   "sources": [
    {
     "label": "Audio script",
     "text": "I practiced my science presentation for my little brother yesterday. I expected him to understand because I had used many pictures. But he asked what several words meant, and I noticed that I had not explained them. I did not remove the important ideas. Instead, I replaced some difficult words with familiar ones and added one everyday example. When I tried again, he could explain the main point back to me. This taught me that checking what the listener understands is more useful than simply asking whether a presentation looks attractive. I will ask another person to listen before the final presentation."
    }
   ],
