     "label": "Audio script",
     "text": "Our class discussed whether everyone should use a tablet for every lesson. Some students liked being able to find information quickly and enlarge text. Others said that notifications could interrupt their concentration and that drawing some diagrams was easier on paper. We realized that a choice between always using tablets and never using them was too simple. The class proposed using tablets when their features helped the task, while keeping paper available for other activities. We also agreed to turn off unnecessary notifications. Next month, we will ask students which tasks became easier and which problems remained, rather than assuming the new plan works equally well for everyone."
