     "label": "Audio script",
     "text": "A student team helped a cafe test reusable cups for drinks taken outside. Customers paid a small deposit and got it back when they returned the cup. During the first week, many cups were not returned. The team first thought people did not care about reuse. After asking customers, however, they learned that the return point was difficult to find and closed too early. The cafe added a clearly marked return box with longer hours. More cups came back during the next week. The team learned that if we want people to change their habits, we should examine practical obstacles instead of immediately blaming their attitudes."
