   "id": "listen-charityreport",
   "level": 3,
   "title": "Reporting a Charity Event",
   "mode": "listen",
   "sources": [
    {
     "label": "Audio script",
     "text": "After our charity event, we wanted to report that it had been a complete success. We had sold all the handmade cards and raised more money than last year. But some volunteers said the preparation had taken so much time that they struggled to finish their homework. We decided our report should include both the amount raised and the volunteers' experience. For next year, we suggested starting earlier, sharing tasks more evenly, and making fewer kinds of cards. A good result in one area does not mean there are no problems elsewhere. By reporting the difficulties as well as the achievements, we hope the next team can plan an event that works better for everyone."
    }
   ],
